#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:5
msgid "What's New in |gf| 5.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:7
msgid ""
"The main contribution of this version is a series of corrections and a few "
"optimizations following an analysis of the code with Claude AI."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:9
msgid "Released version, 2026/11/27."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:11
msgid "The main changes are:"
msgstr "主な変更点は次のとおりです．"

#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:13
msgid "A series of bug fixes and code improvements."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:15
msgid ""
"In GWFL, the term 'Normal' now also refers to the unit normal in the "
"interior of a codimension 1 element (1D element in 2D, and 2D element in "
"3D)."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:17
msgid ""
"The new GWFL term 'element_curvature' gives the Euclidean components of the "
"curvature tensor in such codimension 1 elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:19
msgid "Raytracing for contact conditions extended to shell elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:21
msgid ""
"A better account of tensor symmetry and tensor sparsity in the optimization "
"of elementary computations in the generic assembly."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/whatsnew/5.6.rst:23
msgid ""
"The Octave/Matlab interface plot facilities have been ported to the Python "
"interface."
msgstr ""
